From f325afc269b14f802d2ae5792eab5636e2880996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Rosenfeld <arsfeld@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:18:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add SPLIT_TUNNEL_GID split-tunnel mode

When SPLIT_TUNNEL_GID is set, only sockets owned by that group use the
VPN. Gluetun joins the group itself so its own traffic follows. The rest
of the container keeps its routes, DNS and an unfiltered firewall.

- internal/splittunnel builds the mangle, filter and nat rules and the
  policy routing, with unit tests.
- The firewall keeps ACCEPT policies and only filters marked traffic.
- Wireguard routes the split mark instead of everything but its own mark.
- OpenVPN's redirect-gateway routes move out of the main table.
- The DNS server listens on 127.0.0.1 and resolv.conf is left alone.
